menu "Neo2 Buddy Configuration"

config SUPPORT_BATTERY
    bool "Enable battery support"
    default y
    help
      Enable voltage sensing and battery percentage reporting. When disabled
      battery-related code and UI features will be omitted.

config SUPPORT_SDCARD
    bool "Enable microSD card support"
    default y
    help
      Enable mounting and use of an external microSD card. When disabled the
      SD mount attempts are omitted and only internal flash storage is used.

config SUPPORT_OLED
    bool "Enable 1.3in OLED status display"
    default y
    help
      Build with OLED support for a small on-device status display. When
      disabled only the web UI (if enabled) or UART will be available for status.

config SUPPORT_WIFI_WEB
    bool "Enable Wi-Fi and web portal"
    default y
    help
      SoftAP/STA Wi-Fi, captive DNS, HTTP portal, and cloud sync. When disabled
      the buddy is UART + Neo USB only (no network stack for the portal).

config SUPPORT_BLE
    bool "Enable Bluetooth HID keyboard"
    default y
    help
      NimBLE HID keyboard for Neo key passthrough and portal text relay.
      Disable to shrink the image and free internal DRAM (also unset BT in
      the matching sdkconfig profile fragment).

config SUPPORT_STOCK_APPLETS
    bool "Enable Applet Store (bundled SmartApplets)"
    default y
    depends on SUPPORT_WIFI_WEB
    help
      Embed stock .OS3KApp binaries and expose the portal Applet Store and
      Flash Cards deck library. Requires the web portal.

config BUDDY_RUN_SELF_TEST
    bool "Run boot self-test suite"
    default y
    help
      Run lightweight smoke tests once at boot and log results to the
      device log buffer. Disable to shorten boot time after validation.

config BUDDY_UART_CMD
    bool "Enable protected UART command console"
    default y
    help
      Start an interactive command line on the serial port (115200). Use
      "login <password>" (same as the web portal) before Neo USB commands.
      Intended for development and automated testing over the CH340 UART.

config BUDDY_NEO_LINK
    bool "Enable Neo Link HID transport (archived — do not enable)"
    default n
    help
      ARCHIVED / ABANDONED. Neo OS takes over with "emulating keyboard" while
      USB is plugged; SmartApplets cannot keep a live chat UI. Sources remain
      under archive/neo-link/ for research only. Leave this off.

config BUDDY_NEO_LINK_AUTO_INSTALL_APPLET
    bool "Auto-install/replace Neo Link Chat applet when Neo connects"
    default n
    depends on BUDDY_NEO_LINK
    help
      When enabled and the Neo is already in ASM/comms mode, compare the installed
      Neo Link Chat applet (0xA1C0) to the firmware bundle and replace if missing
      or outdated. Does not run on keyboard-mode plug-in (no automatic ASM flip).
      Default off — use UART/portal `link install` when you change the applet.

endmenu
